#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:198
msgid "Node types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:200
msgid "`node.type`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:202
msgid ""
"A string representation of the selector type. It can be one of the "
"following; `attribute`, `class`, `combinator`, `comment`, `id`, "
"`nesting`, `pseudo`, `root`, `selector`, `string`, `tag`, or `universal`."
" Note that for convenience, these constants are exposed on the main "
"`parser` as uppercased keys. So for example you can get `id` by querying "
"`parser.ID`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:213
msgid "`node.parent`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:215
msgid "Returns the parent node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:221
msgid "`node.toString()`, `String(node)`, or `'' + node`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:223
msgid "Returns a string representation of the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:231
msgid "`node.next()` & `node.prev()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:233
msgid "Returns the next/previous child of the parent node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:242
msgid "`node.replaceWith(node)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:244
msgid "Replace a node with another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:254
msgid "`node`: The node to substitute the original with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:256
msgid "`node.remove()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:258
msgid "Removes the node from its parent node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:266
msgid "`node.clone()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:268
msgid ""
"Returns a copy of a node, detached from any parent containers that the "
"original might have had."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:278
msgid "`node.spaces`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:280
msgid ""
"Extra whitespaces around the node will be moved into `node.spaces.before`"
" and `node.spaces.after`. So for example, these spaces will be moved as "
"they have no semantic meaning:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:288
msgid "However, *combinating* spaces will form a `combinator` node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:294
msgid ""
"A `combinator` node may only have the `spaces` property set if the "
"combinator value is a non-whitespace character, such as `+`, `~` or `>`. "
"Otherwise, the combinator value will contain all of the spaces between "
"selectors."
msgstr ""

