#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:334
msgid "Container types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:336
msgid ""
"The `root`, `selector`, and `pseudo` nodes have some helper methods for "
"working with their children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:339
msgid "`container.nodes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:341
msgid "An array of the container's children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:350
msgid "`container.first` & `container.last`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:352
msgid "The first/last child of the container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:359
msgid "`container.at(index)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:361
msgid "Returns the node at position `index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:370
msgid "`index`: The index of the node to return."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:372
msgid "`container.index(node)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:374
msgid "Return the index of the node within its container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:382
msgid "`node`: A node within the current container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:384
msgid "`container.length`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:386
msgid "Proxy to the length of the container's nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:392
msgid "`container` Array iterators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:394
msgid "The container class provides proxies to certain Array methods; these are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:396
msgid "`container.map === container.nodes.map`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:397
msgid "`container.reduce === container.nodes.reduce`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:398
msgid "`container.every === container.nodes.every`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:399
msgid "`container.some === container.nodes.some`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:400
msgid "`container.filter === container.nodes.filter`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:401
msgid "`container.sort === container.nodes.sort`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:403
msgid ""
"Note that these methods only work on a container's immediate children; "
"recursive iteration is provided by `container.walk`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:406
msgid "`container.each(callback)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:408
msgid ""
"Iterate the container's immediate children, calling `callback` for each "
"child. You may return `false` within the callback to break the iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:421
msgid ""
"Note that unlike `Array#forEach()`, this iterator is safe to use whilst "
"adding or removing nodes from the container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:426
#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:442
msgid ""
"`callback (function)`: A function to call for each node, which receives "
"`node` and `index` arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:429
msgid "`container.walk(callback)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:431
msgid ""
"Like `container#each`, but will also iterate child nodes as long as they "
"are `container` types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:445
msgid ""
"This iterator is safe to use whilst mutating `container.nodes`, like "
"`container#each`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:448
msgid "`container.walk` proxies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:450
msgid ""
"The container class provides proxy methods for iterating over types of "
"nodes, so that it is easier to write modules that target specific "
"selectors. Those methods are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:454
msgid "`container.walkAttributes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:455
msgid "`container.walkClasses`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:456
msgid "`container.walkCombinators`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:457
msgid "`container.walkComments`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:458
msgid "`container.walkIds`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:459
msgid "`container.walkNesting`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:460
msgid "`container.walkPseudos`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:461
msgid "`container.walkTags`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:462
msgid "`container.walkUniversals`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:464
msgid "`container.split(callback)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:466
msgid ""
"This method allows you to split a group of nodes by returning `true` from"
" a callback. It returns an array of arrays, where each inner array "
"corresponds to the groups that you created via the callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:481
msgid ""
"`callback (function)`: A function to call for each node, which receives "
"`node` as an argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:484
msgid "`container.prepend(node)` & `container.append(node)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:486
msgid ""
"Add a node to the start/end of the container. Note that doing so will set"
" the parent property of the node to this container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:496
msgid "`node`: The node to add."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:498
msgid "`container.insertBefore(old, new)` & `container.insertAfter(old, new)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:500
msgid "Add a node before or after an existing node in a container:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:513
msgid "`old`: The existing node in the container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:514
msgid "`new`: The new node to add before/after the existing node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:516
msgid "`container.removeChild(node)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:518
msgid ""
"Remove the node from the container. Note that you can also use "
"`node.remove()` if you would like to remove just a single node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:530
msgid "`node`: The node to remove."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:532
msgid "`container.removeAll()` or `container.empty()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:534
msgid "Remove all children from the container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:541
msgid "Root nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:543
msgid ""
"A root node represents a comma separated list of selectors. Indeed, all a"
" root's `toString()` method does is join its selector children with a "
"','. Other than this, it has no special functionality and acts like a "
"container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:547
msgid "`root.trailingComma`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:549
msgid ""
"This will be set to `true` if the input has a trailing comma, in order to"
" support parsing of legacy CSS hacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:552
msgid "Selector nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:554
msgid ""
"A selector node represents a single compound selector. For example, this "
"selector string `h1 h2 h3, [href] > p`, is represented as two selector "
"nodes. It has no special functionality of its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:558
msgid "Pseudo nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:560
msgid ""
"A pseudo selector extends a container node; if it has any parameters of "
"its own (such as `h1:not(h2, h3)`), they will be its children. Note that "
"the pseudo `value` will always contain the colons preceding the pseudo "
"identifier. This is so that both `:before` and `::before` are properly "
"represented in the AST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:565
msgid "Attribute nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:567
msgid "`attribute.quoted`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:569
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if the attribute's value is wrapped in quotation marks, "
"false if it is not. Remains `undefined` if there is no attribute value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:579
msgid "`attribute.qualifiedAttribute`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:581
msgid "Returns the attribute name qualified with the namespace if one is given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:583
msgid "`attribute.offsetOf(part)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:585
msgid ""
"Returns the offset of the attribute part specified relative to the  start"
" of the node of the output string. This is useful in raising  error "
"messages about a specific part of the attribute, especially  in "
"combination with `attribute.sourceIndex`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:590
msgid ""
"Returns `-1` if the name is invalid or the value doesn't exist in this  "
"attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:593
msgid "The legal values for `part` are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:595
msgid "`\"ns\"` - alias for \"namespace\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:596
msgid "`\"namespace\"` - the namespace if it exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:597
msgid "`\"attribute\"` - the attribute name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:598
msgid "`\"attributeNS\"` - the start of the attribute or its namespace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:599
msgid "`\"operator\"` - the match operator of the attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:600
msgid "`\"value\"` - The value (string or identifier)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:601
msgid "`\"insensitive\"` - the case insensitivity flag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:603
msgid "`attribute.raws.unquoted`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:605
msgid ""
"Returns the unquoted content of the attribute's value. Remains "
"`undefined` if there is no attribute value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:615
msgid "`attribute.spaces`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:617
msgid ""
"Like `node.spaces` with the `before` and `after` values containing the "
"spaces around the element, the parts of the attribute can also have "
"spaces before and after them. The for each of `attribute`, `operator`, "
"`value` and `insensitive` there is corresponding property of the same nam"
" in `node.spaces` that has an optional `before` or `after` string "
"containing only whitespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:624
msgid ""
"Note that corresponding values in `attributes.raws.spaces` contain values"
" including any comments. If set, these values will override the "
"`attribute.spaces` value. Take care to remove them if changing "
"`attribute.spaces`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:629
msgid "`attribute.raws`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:631
msgid ""
"The raws object stores comments and other information necessary to re-"
"render the node exactly as it was in the source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:634
msgid ""
"If a comment is embedded within the identifiers for the `namespace`, "
"`attribute` or `value` then a property is placed in the raws for that "
"value containing the full source of the propery including comments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:637
msgid ""
"If a comment is embedded within the space between parts of the attribute "
"then the raw for that space is set accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:640
msgid "Setting an attribute's property `raws` value to be deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:642
msgid ""
"For now, changing the spaces required also updating or removing any of "
"the  raws values that override them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:645
msgid ""
"Example: `[ /*before*/ href /* after-attr */ = /* after-operator */ te"
"/*inside-value*/st/* wow */ /*omg*/i/*bbq*/ /*whodoesthis*/]` would parse"
" as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:673
msgid "`Processor`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:675
msgid "`ProcessorOptions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:677
msgid "`lossless` - When `true`, whitespace is preserved. Defaults to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:678
msgid ""
"`updateSelector` - When `true`, if any processor methods are passed a "
"postcss `Rule` node instead of a string, then that Rule's selector is "
"updated with the results of the processing. Defaults to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:682
msgid "`process|processSync(selectors, [options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:684
msgid ""
"Processes the `selectors`, returning a string from the result of "
"processing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:686
#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:734
#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:743
msgid ""
"Note: when the `updateSelector` option is set, the rule's selector will "
"be updated with the resulting string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:689
msgid "**Example:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:723
msgid ""
"`selectors (string|postcss.Rule)`: Either a selector string or a PostCSS "
"Rule node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:725
msgid "`[options] (object)`: Process options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:728
msgid "`ast|astSync(selectors, [options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:730
msgid ""
"Like `process()` and `processSync()` but after processing the `selectors`"
" these methods return the `Root` node of the result instead of a string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:737
msgid "`transform|transformSync(selectors, [options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-selector-parser_API.md:739
msgid ""
"Like `process()` and `processSync()` but after processing the `selectors`"
